From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:35:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tilelang): own sampler copy and cast kernels

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus candidate-38 (1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4).

Move the sampler generic ATen cast/strided-copy computation into a declared TileLang kernel. Keep the dense FP32 device memcpy path. Processing still receives independent FP32 storage while raw logits remain unchanged, and all subsequent sampling operations retain their original order.

Quality: no sampling arithmetic, RNG, masking, verification or raw-logprob change. Tests cover FP16/BF16/FP32, padded/transposed/column-strided sources, tails, empty shapes, signed zero, infinities and NaNs, input ownership, cache declarations and CUDA replay. Native results are retained in the deployment experiment. Upstream status: local candidate, not submitted.
